    description: "## Origin\n\nFiled per discussion surrounding WI-votut. See sister item `WI-mifif` (Django) — the first-framework PR.\n\n## Gap\n\n`hypergumbo run` on a Spring MVC app produces no `renders` edge connecting a controller method to its view file. The relationship is currently uncovered: a `@Controller`-annotated method that does `return \"users/show\"` resolves to `src/main/resources/templates/users/show.html` (Thymeleaf default) under Spring's view resolver, but no edge captures that link.\n\n## Spring convention to model\n\n- **Action detection**: methods on `@Controller`-annotated classes (NOT `@RestController` — those return JSON, not view names) annotated with `@RequestMapping` or its variants `@GetMapping` / `@PostMapping` / `@PutMapping` / `@DeleteMapping` / `@PatchMapping`.\n- **View name source**: the method's return value is the view name. This is **explicit** (string return), not derived from method name — distinct from Rails/Phoenix/Django CBV-default where the convention is method-name-based.\n  - `return \"users/show\"` → resolve under templates root.\n  - `return \"redirect:/foo\"` → not a view, skip.\n  - `return new ModelAndView(\"users/show\", model)` → first arg is the view name.\n- **Template path derivation**: `<src/main/resources/>templates/<view-name><ext>` for Thymeleaf; `<src/main/webapp/>WEB-INF/views/<view-name>.jsp` for JSP.\n- **Extensions**: `.html` (Thymeleaf), `.jsp`, `.ftl` / `.ftlh` (FreeMarker), `.vm` (Velocity).\n\n## Strategy alignment with shared core\n\nThis linker uses the **explicit-string strategy** exposed by the shared core (assuming WI-mifif lands both strategy hooks per its scope; if not, this PR extracts the explicit-string strategy as its own contribution).\n\n## Coordination with WI-hokaj (Laravel)\n\nSpring and Laravel share the explicit-string strategy. Neither has an `isbefore` on the other; whichever lands first does the actual extraction work (if WI-mifif didn't already set it up), the second is a thin port. The string-arg-of-call detection (Spring: method return statement; Laravel: argument of `view()` call) is the shared kernel, with per-language detection variants.\n\n## Build order\n\nBlocked on WI-mifif merging (shared core extraction).\n\n## Analyzer pre-req\n\nConfirm before scheduling: the Java analyzer correctly extracts `@Controller` annotation, `@RequestMapping` family annotations on methods, AND string-return-value-of-method (the specific AST shape for `return \"users/show\";` inside an annotated method). Sibling lang-mainstream/lang-common analyzer capability could bottleneck.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- A Spring fixture with `@Controller class UserController { @GetMapping(\"/users/{id}\") String show(...) { return \"users/show\"; } }` and `templates/users/show.html` produces a `renders` edge.\n- Method returning `\"redirect:...\"` does not produce a `renders` edge.\n- `@RestController` classes are skipped.\n- `ModelAndView(\"users/show\", model)` first-argument form produces a `renders` edge.\n- 100% coverage on changed source."  # 1e4e
